# CAPTURE of robo-dog's /etc/accretion/ds4-server.env (the ds4/accretion local
# model server, systemd unit ds4-server.service — see ds4-server.service here).
#
# REFRESHED 2026-08-16: this capture had drifted badly from the host. It still
# described the DeepSeek-V4-Flash era (131072 ctx, 70GB cache budget,
# --ssd-streaming flags) while the host had been switched to Inkling-Small.
# That drift is why litellm kept sending "deepseek-v4-flash" to a server that
# serves "inkling-small" — see hosting/services/litellm.yaml.
#
# The SERVED MODEL ID is derived from the model path (here: inkling-small) and
# is what litellm must send. Change the model, change litellm in the same PR.
#
# ACCRETION_ADMIN_TOKEN is deliberately a placeholder — the real value lives on
# the host only and must never be committed.
DS4_MODEL=/data/gguf/models/inkling-small/Inkling-Small-UD-IQ2_XXS.accretion.gguf
DS4_CTX=65536
DS4_CACHE_BUDGET=
DS4_EXTRA_FLAGS=
DS4_KV_PIN_MIN_HITS=2
DS4_EMBD_MMAP=1
DS4_SERVER_MIXED_PREFILL_QUANTUM=2048
DS4_ENV_FILE=/etc/accretion/ds4-server.env
DS4_MODEL_DIRS=/home/jacinta/src/ds4/gguf:/data/gguf:/data/gguf/models/inkling-small
DS4_ARCH=inkling
ACCRETION_ARCH_WRAPPER=1
ACCRETION_ADMIN_TOKEN=REDACTED-SEE-HOST
